data optional_equality_answers_by_representation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "optional_equality_answers_by_representation" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: `xs.first() == Present { value: X }` answers false when the list's first element is X. Two optionals compared, both meaning Present X, and the interpreter answers unequal. The comparison is T? == T?, so the wall of optional_compared_with_required_value (EqualityOptionalityMismatch, gunbc#13179) admits it, correctly: it has one meaning.",

    "ROOT, NOT A NEW EVALUATOR DEFECT: the interpreter realizes `first` as the raw element or Null, while emitted Rust realizes it as Optional<T> (gunbc.cli_dispatch_surface; known red test.claim.cli_dispatch_surface interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional, already in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red). The read hands equality a bare X, the literal is Present X, and equality answers by representation, the arm optional_compared_with_required_value already records. So the earliest unjustified boundary (DESIGN 6b) is the interpreter's `first` producing a value that is not the modeled optional. Equality and the checker are downstream consequences.",

    "WHAT THIS ROW ADDS IS THE HARM ROUTE. EqualityOptionalityMismatch tells the author to compare against `Present { value: .. }` first, so following the compiler's own remedy for a refused T? == T walks straight into this divergence and gets a silently false Bool. Measured 2026-10-07 on gunbc.os_install_actuator_selection srv3_os_install_actuator_host_selected_because_requirements_and_policy: rewritten that way, the production predicate went false. gunbc#13536 matches on the optional instead.",

    "EVIDENCE BY EXECUTION: test.claim.optional_equality_by_representation. RED a_present_first_equals_its_present_literal is `.first()` over a data list of variant rows, compared with a Present literal. It is enrolled in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red, so it executes on every floor and is held as known-red. POSITIVE CONTROL a_match_on_the_present_first_reads_its_value is the same read eliminated by a match, an ordinary claim. First observed as probes zz_a1 (FAIL) and zz_c1 (PASS) over test.claim.os_install_actuator_selection at gunbc#13536's base.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder on the interpretation path. CEILING: 4. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: one authority for `first` from which the interpreter and the emitted realization are both derived, so the interpreter's `first` yields the modeled optional on every route (method form and pipe form). When it lands, both enrolled reds (this one and interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional) pass, their roster rows are deleted, and the claims remain as regression controls (DESIGN 4b(4)). Until then, the interim discipline at a `first` read is to match on the optional.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.optional_compared_with_required_value", decl_name: "optional_compared_with_required_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cli_dispatch_surface", decl_name: "interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.optional_equality_by_representation", decl_name: "a_present_first_equals_its_present_literal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.optional_equality_by_representation", decl_name: "a_match_on_the_present_first_reads_its_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.os_install_actuator_selection", decl_name: "srv3_os_install_actuator_host_selected_because_requirements_and_policy", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
